The '''Gran Presa del Nord''' ({{lang|ca|Gran Presa del Nord}}; "Great Dam of the North") is a hydroelectric dam on the southern shore of [[Lake Iwarakí]] in the [[La Serra de Llevant]] comarca of [[Tramuntana Province]], [[Balboa]]. Operated by the [[Corporació Hidroelèctrica de Balboa]] (CHB), it is one of the largest dams in the Yalabirga hydroelectric network and a major source of electricity for the northern highlands.

== History ==

The Gran Presa del Nord was constructed as part of the post-reunification expansion of Balboa's hydroelectric capacity during the 1970s and 1980s. The [[Corporació Hidroelèctrica de Balboa]] identified [[Lake Iwarakí]] as a suitable site for a major dam due to the lake's natural basin, substantial surface area, and favourable topography for hydroelectric generation. Construction began in 1974 and the dam was completed in 1979.

The dam was built at the lake's natural southern outflow, raising the water level and converting the natural lake into a regulated reservoir. The project was one of the largest infrastructure undertakings in Tramuntana Province during the expansion period and brought significant employment and infrastructure investment to the [[La Serra de Llevant]] comarca, transforming the nearby town of [[Sant Jorge, Tramuntana|Sant Jorge]] into the primary service centre for the comarca.

The dam's construction affected [[Birú people|Birú]] communities in the surrounding highlands, contributing to the broader pattern of indigenous displacement associated with the Yalabirga hydroelectric expansion. Opposition from environmental groups and Birú communities to further dam construction in the highlands contributed to the government's decision to pursue nuclear power through the establishment of [[Organització d'Energia Nuclear de Balboa|OENB]] in 1998.

== Operation ==

The Gran Presa del Nord regulates the outflow from [[Lake Iwarakí]] into the [[Yalabirga River]]. The dam's hydroelectric station generates electricity from the controlled release of water through the reservoir. Generation is seasonal, with peak output during the wet season (May to November) when inflow is highest, and reduced output during the dry season.

The dam is operated by the [[Corporació Hidroelèctrica de Balboa]] (CHB) as part of the broader Yalabirga hydroelectric network, which includes the original 1964 dam at [[Llac de la Boira]] and other dams constructed during the 1970s and 1980s expansion.

